Drop the toolbox status bar

Removes the "Opens in a new tab - searches this topic" strip and the rule
above it. It was a caption explaining behaviour the user finds out by
clicking once, printed permanently under five buttons that are each two
words long.

The per-button title attributes still say what each destination is for,
which is the half of that line worth keeping and only appears when asked
for.

The buttons row is now the shade's direct child. window-shade > * carries
the clipping, so the wrapper existed only to hold the two rows together.
